  <div class="g2" style="margin-top:24px;align-items:start">
   <div>
    <p>Travel labor is the borrow play, run as a managed service. AFIMAC sources, screens, travels, houses, and supervises a team, then deploys them to your site for the length of the situation. The crew draws from a national network of 20,000+ workers instead of one local market. Safety onboarding is done before the first shift, and the team works under AFIMAC supervision with a single point of contact. There’s no long-term commitment; when the gap closes, demobilization is part of the plan.</p>
    <p>For most roles, that’s a working crew within days of a signed plan. The difference isn’t just speed. It’s that nothing about the crew lands on your managers while they’re already fighting the gap that caused the problem.</p>
